{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אנכי", :translit "anokhi", :gloss "I"} {:he "כסא לו", :translit "kissei lo", :gloss "a throne to Him / His throne"} {:he "מלא", :translit "malei", :gloss "full / fills"} {:he "הלא את השמים ואת הארץ אני מלא", :translit "halo et ha-shamayim v'et ha-aretz ani malei", :gloss "Do I not fill heaven and earth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אנכי", :b "כסא לו"} {:kind :gematria, :a "אנכי", :b "מלא ועוד עשרה"} {:kind :other, :note "Ten Divine Names identified within the word אנכי, mapped spatially to heaven, earth, four directions, depth, and height"}], :frame {:text "Jeremiah 23:24 records God's declaration, 'Do I not fill heaven and earth?' The verse is applied to the word אנכי at the start of the Decalogue to express that God's presence permeates all of creation. The phrase 'first and last in heaven and on earth' echoes Isaiah 57:15, where God is described as 'high and exalted, inhabiting eternity, whose name is Holy One,' dwelling simultaneously in the heights and with the contrite.", :sources ["Jeremiah 23:24" "Isaiah 57:15"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשר הוצאתיך", :translit "asher hotzeitikha", :gloss "who brought you out"} {:he "אשר הוצאתיך", :translit "asher hotzeitikha", :gloss "who brought you out"} {:he "אשר הוצאתיך מאור כשדים", :translit "asher hotzeitikha me'ur kasdim", :gloss "who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["אשר הוצאתיך" "אשר הוצאתיך" "אשר הוצאתיך מאור כשדים"]}], :frame {:text "Genesis 15:7 records God's words to Abraham: 'I am the Lord who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees.' Ba'al HaTurim reads the three-fold Masoretic occurrence of 'אשר הוצאתיך' as linking the Exodus from Egypt to the earlier departure from Ur: just as God removed Abraham from Ur, so He removed Israel from Egypt, in each case to bring them to receive Torah.", :sources ["Genesis 15:7"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "אנכי", :a-value 81, :b "כסא לו", :b-value 117,